    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/kg-viewer.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The page is generated, not committed",
      "prov:value": "The page is `<site>/<stub>/index.html` and reads `../<name>/<stub>.jsonld` (the document's own path, under its instance's directory, the host's included, since 2026-10-23), so the same bytes work on the canonical site and under `branches/<slug>/` with no configuration, no `--base-url`, and no build-time branch.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/kg-viewer.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every asset has its own IRI — a materialized path, loading published JSON-LD",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-02 (#1881), in order: *\"404 githubpages is a hack. does not work according to stanrds\"*; *\"each link/page needs to be materialized on the CDN (gh-pagees), just load the content from the KG json(ld) assets already published\"*; *\"no query strings... each asset gets its own IRI\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "Owner",
        "#1881",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/kg-viewer.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The asset and its rendering are two resources with two IRIs",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-02 (#1881): *\"each asset should have one IRI, but the view page is a rendering of that asset, a different page. fix IRIs\"*; and, against putting `schema:subjectOf` on the asset, *\"hard to maintain? asset doesnt know about its renderings\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "Owner",
        "#1881",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
